.TH PUPPETC-CA 1 "January 2026" "puppetc 0.0.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
puppetc-ca \- Certificate Authority management for puppetc
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B puppetc-ca
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] <\fIcommand\fR> [\fIargs\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B puppetc-ca
is a command-line tool for managing the puppetc Certificate Authority.
It allows administrators to list, sign, revoke, and inspect certificates
and certificate signing requests (CSRs).
.PP
This tool is primarily used when autosigning is disabled on the server
and manual certificate approval is required.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-ca\-dir " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to CA directory. Default: \fB/etc/puppetc/ssl/ca\fR
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help message and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List all certificates (both pending CSRs and signed certificates).
.TP
.B list \-\-pending
List only pending Certificate Signing Requests.
.TP
.B list \-\-signed
List only signed certificates.
.TP
.B sign \fIcertname\fR
Sign a pending CSR for the specified certname.
.TP
.B sign \-\-all
Sign all pending CSRs.
.TP
.B revoke \fIcertname\fR
Revoke (delete) a signed certificate.
.TP
.B clean \fIcertname\fR
Remove a pending CSR without signing it.
.TP
.B print \fIcertname\fR
Print the contents of a certificate or CSR in PEM format.
.SH FILES
The CA directory contains the following structure:
.TP
.I ca_crt.pem
CA certificate
.TP
.I ca_key.pem
CA private key
.TP
.I serial
Serial number counter for signed certificates
.TP
.I requests/
Directory containing pending CSRs (\fI<certname>.pem\fR)
.TP
.I signed/
Directory containing signed certificates (\fI<certname>.pem\fR)
.SH EXAMPLES
List all certificates:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-ca list
.RE
.PP
List only pending CSRs:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-ca list \-\-pending
.RE
.PP
Sign a specific certificate request:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-ca sign webserver1.example.com
.RE
.PP
Sign all pending requests:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-ca sign \-\-all
.RE
.PP
Revoke a certificate:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-ca revoke old\-server.example.com
.RE
.PP
View certificate details:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-ca print webserver1.example.com
.RE
.PP
Use a custom CA directory:
.PP
.RS
puppetc-ca \-C /opt/puppet/ssl/ca list
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
Error (certificate not found, signing failed, etc.)
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR puppetc-server (1),
.BR puppetc-agent (1),
.BR openssl (1)
